 R←Test_Select_013(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;⎕IO;⎕ML;list;qdmx;value
⍝ Exercise "Select" with `quitFlag` as fourth positional parameter.
⍝ Only the checks carried out on the left argument and automation are exercised here:
⍝ the selection itself needs a user, see "Test_Select_014".
⍝ The parameter was introduced in 3.1.0
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 ⎕IO←1 ⋄ ⎕ML←1
 R←T._Failed

 list←'One' 'Two' 'Three'

 ⍝ Invalid specifications of "quitFlag":
 :For value :In 2(,1)'x'(0 1)
     :Trap 11
         {}('Select one:' 0 1 value)C.Select list
         →T.GoToTidyUp 1
     :Else
         qdmx←⎕DMX
         →T.GoToTidyUp'"quitFlag" must be a Boolean'≢qdmx.EM
     :EndTrap
 :EndFor

 ⍝ Automation is not restricted by "quitFlag": "q" always returns ¯1:
 C.AddAutomation'Select' 'Select one:' 'q'
 →T.GoToTidyUp ¯1≢('Select one:' 0 1 1)C.Select list
 →T.GoToTidyUp ¯1≢('Select one:' 0 1 0)C.Select list
 →T.GoToTidyUp ¯1≢('Select one:' 0 0 0)C.Select list
 →T.GoToTidyUp ¯1≢('Select one:' 0 1)C.Select list
 →T.GoToTidyUp 4≠C.∆Automation[1;4]

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 C.Cleanup
⍝Done
